    "choosing_definition": [
      "1. Start with the most specific evidence source available (ICD + lab > self-report alone)",
      "2. Use ≥2 independent sources when possible (UKB 'probable' standard)",
      "3. Always document exclusion criteria — what you exclude is as important as what you include",
      "4. Specify time window: prevalent (already has disease) vs incident (develops disease during follow-up)",
      "5. List ALL variables used to define the outcome — these CANNOT be predictors (MLGG-F01)",
      "6. If using composite definitions, perform sensitivity analysis with each component separately",
      "7. Report validation metrics: concordance between sources, positive predictive value if available"
