    "common_pitfalls": [
      "Using HbA1c to define diabetes AND as a predictor (circular logic / guaranteed leakage)",
      "Including ICD codes for the target condition as features (e.g., E11 code + predict diabetes)",
      "Not distinguishing prevalent from incident cases (mixing existing and new cases)",
      "Ignoring competing risks (death prevents readmission — cannot treat death as 'no readmission')",
      "Using self-report alone without corroboration (low specificity, recall bias)",
      "Not excluding conditions that mimic the target (e.g., T1D misclassified as T2D)",
